---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About · The Consensus Field Guide"
  description="What the Consensus Field Guide is for, and how to read it."
  nav="about"
>
  <div class="wrap-narrow prose about">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1>A field guide, not a textbook</h1>
    <p>
      Blockchain consensus moves fast, and most of what's written about it is either a 40-page paper or a one-line
      marketing claim. This guide sits in between. Its goal is to take a curious engineer from "how do strangers agree
      at all?" to the protocols being published today.
    </p>

    <h2>How to read it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>The family tree</strong> is the map. Every protocol appears once, placed by when it appeared and which
        family it belongs to. Lines show which earlier ideas each one built on.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Lessons</strong> are the depth. Each has an interactive model or guided scenario (try a fault or advance one step at a time), the one idea it added, what it gave up, and a couple of questions to check yourself.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>About the animations</h2>
    <p>
      The simulations and guided walkthroughs are teaching models, not implementations. They use small examples and
      simplified rules to explain each protocol. The guided scenarios are scripted traces, not exhaustive protocol
      simulators; each states what it leaves out. Playback starts paused and advances every six seconds by default,
      with slower and faster options and a manual Step button. Each lesson links to the
      original papers and specifications, which are the authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Spotted a mistake?</h2>
    <p>Corrections are welcome. If you spot a mistake, please <a href="https://github.com/rootulp/consensus-field-guide/issues">create an issue on GitHub</a>. Include the lesson, what looks wrong, and a link to the relevant paper or specification if you have one.</p>

    <p><a href="/">Back to the family tree →</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

